# INFRA-10: `.gitignore` bularni allaqachon tashlab ketadi, lekin `builder`
# bosqichi `COPY . .` ishlatadi — `.dockerignore`da bo'lmasa build
# konteksti/qatlamiga (image cache'iga) kirib qoladi. `.claude/` va
# `audit/` server tafsilotlari va zaiflik topilmalarini o'z ichiga oladi
# (README: "umumiy repo'ga tushmasligi kerak" — image qatlami ham shunday).
.claude
audit
eval-out
scratch-tmp
docs
# scripts/backup.sh BACKUP_ENV_FILE (R2a re-review): belt-and-braces —
# standart joyi repo/build kontekstidan tashqarida (/etc/slaydx/backup.env),
# lekin shu nomdagi fayl repo ichida qolib ketsa ham `builder`ning
# `COPY . .` orqali image qatlamiga (BACKUP_REMOTE/TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN) kirmasin.
.backup.env
*.backup.env
# Ops sprint (docs/ops/O1-deploy-pipeline.md §3.2): not needed by `next build`
# or by any runtime stage. In the context they only invalidate `COPY . .` (a
# test-only commit re-ran the whole `next build`) and Next file tracing could
# drag them into `standalone/`. KEEP in the context: `scripts/` (`npm run
# build` runs `scripts/guard-build.mjs`; the worker runs `scripts/*.ts`),
# `data/`, `public/`, `brand/`, `lib/` (incl. `lib/server/migrations`), `app/`,
# `components/`, `tsconfig.json`, `next.config.ts`, `postcss.config.mjs`,
# `eslint.config.mjs`. `tests/docker-image-slim.test.mts` locks both lists.
tests
loadtests
